  "map_id": "map:pierre-auger-observatory",
  "method": "80 of the 1587 active main-array stations: the active sd1500 stations sorted by northing from north to south and split into 20 consecutive groups of 79 or 80, so that each record stays within 400 vertices; this group lies between UTM northing 6115.2 km and 6117.8 km. Station positions are the northing and easting columns of sdMap.csv in the Pierre Auger Collaboration Open Data release 3 (20 March 2024, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.10488964), which the Collaboration describes as \"UTC\" [sic] coordinates in metres (the data page does not state the zone or datum). They are read as UTM zone 19 south (central meridian 69 deg W) on the WGS 84 ellipsoid (EPSG:32719) because only zone 19 puts the numbers at Malargue (the converted stations span latitude 34.93 to 35.52 S and longitude 68.91 to 69.66 W), and WGS 84 is the GPS datum; this reading is this work's assumption, hence confidence approximate and accuracy_m 50. Only stations the release marks as still in operation (stop = 1) are drawn; 53 stations with a recorded stop time are not. Each station is drawn as a 3.6 m square centred on its position, aligned to true north: the tank diameter of 3.6 m is from the Observatory paper (arXiv:1502.01323 section 3.1), so the marker has the real tank size, not the tank outline. Check done in the worklog: nearest-neighbour distance of the 1587 active sd1500 stations has a median of 1489.5 m against the official triangular grid of 1500 m (arXiv:1502.01323 section 1); station altitudes in the table run 1344 m to 1619 m against the official 1340 m to 1610 m.",
  "name": "Auger SD1500 stations, band 6 of 20 (north to south)",
  "notes": [
    "The 22 stations flagged both sd1500 and sd750 are drawn here with the main array (they sit on the 1500 m grid and are also part of the infill)."
  ],
  "representation": "surveyed",
  "schema": "hep-atlas/0.2",
  "site_id": "site:malargue-auger",
